Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 18:30:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] main/pcre2: no JIT on riscv32

On the ESP32-S31 (rv32imac, ilp32), code generated by the JIT faults
with an illegal-instruction trap on its first instruction, a valid
c.addi16sp, while the same patterns match with pcre2grep --no-jit. The
likely cause is that the instruction cache is not synchronised with the
freshly written code on that SoC; it is not fixed by userspace.

Build without JIT on riscv32, as on sh, and bump pkgrel so installed
copies get replaced. glib and other users fall back to the interpreter.
---
 main/pcre2/APKBUILD | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/main/pcre2/APKBUILD b/main/pcre2/APKBUILD
index a6fc029f2fe..b9b51587a37 100644
--- a/main/pcre2/APKBUILD
+++ b/main/pcre2/APKBUILD
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 # Maintainer: Jakub Jirutka <jakub@jirutka.cz>
 pkgname=pcre2
 pkgver=10.49
-pkgrel=0
+pkgrel=1
 pkgdesc="Perl-compatible regular expression library"
 url="https://pcre.org/"
 arch="all"
@@ -42,7 +42,9 @@ source="https://github.com/PCRE2Project/pcre2/releases/download/pcre2-$pkgver/pc
 #     - CVE-2022-1587
 
 case "$CARCH" in
-	sh*) _enable_jit="";;
+	# riscv32: JIT code dies with SIGILL on its first instruction on the
+	# ESP32-S31 (rv32imac); the interpreter works
+	sh*|riscv32) _enable_jit="";;
 	*) _enable_jit="--enable-jit";;
 esac
 
